FINDINGS #C1174 tip df8b862b: L1 (low) any --config file's own folder is still an upload root.

fileRoots is now trusted only from the owner's config, with home from os.userInfo, which is right. But rootsFor still returns dirname(real) for ANY --config, so the card's goal ('a config an agent wrote cannot widen the folders') does not hold: an agent writes, or simply names, any JSON file in another folder (say ~/Desktop/x.json, or an existing .json beside private PDFs), and that folder becomes a root. The dot-part check covers only the parts BELOW the root, so even a dot folder can be the root. Then put-file uploads a .pdf, .txt, .csv or picture from there to the board. The other checks still apply (no 0600 files, no secret-looking names, the type list, no hard links) and the host is still the owner's, hence low. Fix: when the config is not one the owner's hooks name, refuse ('this config is not the owner's board config'), or give it no roots at all. Add a test: a non-owner config in another folder cannot upload a file beside it.

